        "avatar": "https://cdn1.telesco.pe/file/p_reSMUGKW7LRnqdaEdo_3O8yS4u4Jgw3B8RKkt4lXY0R3xvMALymUrTk6oSzx-GPyoDEdweqAVNSo-32T2osWhObc6CtMn49cib__Wj0rsKSgvB6Jh-2-VYsQZS8dLI_i04GWqLKJNODYSZHfuyu40n_AadIIxV_JVFxzbzWDL9wN_wK04EEqm0LSpB0M6_kVPwLjUpkLVAhnIgrxZEpOOZ_ujVBaPTGgOjSt-gM6QfLDEKwfAKCRspVIRwFnf-dt94CCHZos1HOVb-gTDN4dYWPVRg6ua_VLFprc9Wq3ASo4NSyX68VzahqmvYJ4xlkKldkIA21Puxf3IWPirBYg.jpg"
      },
      "sourceId": "us:cisco",
      "sourceCountryCode": "us",
      "contentType": "text",
      "media": [],
      "hasMediaInOriginal": false,
      "fallbackReason": null,
      "text": "Multiple Cisco Products Snort 3 Denial of Service Vulnerability\nhttps://sec.cloudapps.cisco.com/security/center/content/CiscoSecurityAdvisory/cisco-sa-snort3-gtpcodec-dos-Rmecfepz?vs_f=Cisco%20Security%20Advisory%26vs_cat=Security%20Intelligence%26vs_type=RSS%26vs_p=Multiple%20Cisco%20Products%20Snort%203%20Denial%20of%20Service%20Vulnerability%26vs_k=1\n\nMultiple Cisco products are affected by a vulnerability in the Snort 3 Detection Engine that could allow an unauthenticated, remote attacker to cause the detection engine to unexpectedly restart, resulting in a denial of service (DoS) condition.\nThe vulnerability is due to a flaw in logic handling when General Packet Radio Service (GPRS) Tunneling Protocol (GTP) extension headers are processed within the codec. An attacker could exploit this vulnerability by sending a crafted, fragmented UDP datagram that contains these headers to the Snort 3 Detection Engine of an affected device. A successful exploit could allow the attacker to cause the detection engine to enter an infinite loop, resulting in a DoS condition.\n\nCisco has released software updates that address this vulnerability. There are workarounds that address this vulnerability.\nThis advisory is available at the following link:\nhttps://sec.cloudapps.cisco.com/security/center/content/CiscoSecurityAdvisory/cisco-sa-snort3-gtpcodec-dos-Rmecfepz\nThis advisory is part of a group of advisories. For a complete list of the advisories and links to them, see Cisco Advance Notification for Publication of October 21, 2026, Security Advisories (https://sec.cloudapps.cisco.com/security/center/content/CiscoSecurityAdvisory/cisco-sa-notice-QGwHnJ6k). In addition, for further documentation of improvements and fixes in Open Source Snort 3, see Multiple Cisco Products Snort 3 Security Hardening Release: October 2026 (https://sec.cloudapps.cisco.com/security/center/content/CiscoSecurityAdvisory/cisco-sa-hardening-snort3-ybgmhTQe).\n         \n             Security Impact Rating:  Medium\n      \n      \n          CVE: CVE-2026-76445",
